      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T17:41:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, we add -Wno-error\u003dunused-... as a no-override flag - it cannot be silenced by any project.  Every project sees the warning but it\u0027s not an error.  The goal is to eventually fix the warnings and use -Werror\u003dunused-... instead.\n\nSince we can\u0027t fix all external projects, aosp/1922839 tries to create an exception for them but looks like it doesn\u0027t help because the flags are in the wrong order `-Wno-unused-... -Wno-error\u003dunused...`. \n\nThis CL makes the flags be `-Wno-error\u003dunused... -Wno-unused...` for external projects by creating an additional no-override flag category that only applies to external projects.  As a consequence, external projects cannot opt into this warning at all.\n\nI think with extra work in the build system, we could add -Wno-foo as an external no-override flag iff -Wfoo is not in `local.{cflags,cppflags}` (see builder.go:482 in this CL) but I am not sure if exposing this option is worth the extra complexity.",
      "parentUuid": "c07a7a22_93d8d7cd",
      "revId": "e24303f71ae13fae7b5b805196487731dde09be8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9aa858b_dfd70551",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
